# Decimal comparisons promote mixed operands

Verifies decimal comparisons accept int, double and float operands in both
operand orders without losing precision. Every value is exactly
representable in all three representations.

>>> source
narrow_int: int = 5
narrow_double: double = 5
narrow_float: float = 5
wide: decimal = 10

print(narrow_int < wide)
print(wide <= narrow_double)
print(narrow_float > wide)
print(wide >= narrow_int)
print(narrow_double == wide)
print(wide != narrow_float)

<<< stdout
true
false
false
true
false
true

<<< stderr
